<!--
    decbench NOVEL pool, `(code *)` cluster (cluster record
    docs/decbench/triage/novel-code-ptr-cluster.md; witness
    O2-noinline-crazyflie-cf2-dwHandleInterrupt @ 0x804001c).

    Every ARM/Thumb indirect call was emitted with an ISA-mode bit-clear the
    source never performs, and the mask blocked the function-pointer type from
    reaching the load:

        (*(code *)(*(uint4 *)(a0 + 0x44) &amp; 0xfffffffe))(a0)   // kuna, before
        (**(code **)(param_1 + 0x44))(param_1)                 // ghidra

    SLEIGH lowers every Thumb indirect call through `BXWritePC`
    (ARM.sinc:221), whose second line is `local tmp = addr &amp; 0xfffffffe`, so
    an INT_AND feeds the CALLIND target.  Upstream erases that AND in
    `RuleFuncPtrEncoding` (decompiler/cpp/ruleaction.cc:9928) whenever the
    compiler spec declares `&lt;funcptr align="N"/&gt;`.  kuna's port of the rule was
    complete but its only input was a hard-coded `funcptr_align() = 0` stub, so
    the rule could never fire on any architecture.

    Stage model: P3 dataflow, simplification quiescence: the rule pool entry
    `funcptrencoding` in `p3_dataflow/ruleaction_8.rs`.

    No option: this is a strict bug fix (finishing a stubbed port).  The
    processor cspec, not kuna, declares the alignment; upstream honours it; the
    emitted C stated an operation the program does not perform.

    Pass 1 (ARM Thumb, `&lt;funcptr align="2"/&gt;` in ARM.cspec) is the FIX: the
    dispatcher's `blx r3` renders with no mask and the field types as `code **`.
    Pass 2 re-runs the same function with `option thumbfuncptr off`, the other
    live reader of `funcptr_align` (GH-8471 / DIV-2, `p3_dataflow/ruleaction_6.rs`
    `RulePtrsubUndo::preserve_thumb_funcptr`): the two features touch the same
    low bit from opposite ends, and the mask must stay stripped either way.

    Layout (hand-laid Thumb-2, the reduced crazyflie `dwHandleInterrupt` shape):
       0x10100  dispatch:  push {r4,lr}; mov r4,r0; ldr r3,[r0,#4]
                           cmp r3,#0; beq +1; mov r0,r4; blx r3
                           pop {r4,pc}
-->
